as you all know trooper micah may will  be laid to rest later this morning he  died  after being hit by a carjacking suspect  on the i-15 during a chaotic  police chase he was laying down spike  strips trying to stop the suspect's  rampage  so here's a look at how the community  will remember him  paying tribute to nevada highway patrol  trooper micah may  the 46 year old was killed in the line  of duty on july 27  while trying to stop a suspected  carjacker the trooper fought for his  life at umc  hospital but did not survive it left the  local law enforcement community  devastated it's these tragic situations  like this where  you really realize that las vegas is a  community it's a community that cares  trooper may was a husband and father of  two young children  on tuesday hundreds gathered at police  memorial park in the northwest valley  for a candlelight vigil may's wife  shared how much he loved his family  and how proud he was to protect and  serve the community michael loved his  job  and he loved being a straight trooper he  found great joy  in taking bad people off the road i know  that he gave his life doing what he  loved he  came to work every day and he did his  job but yet when the chips were down he  was the first guy responding and the  first person on scene  the procession will begin at 9 30 at  palm mortuary on main street  it will end at central church where the  funeral service starts  at 11. heard again there will be several  road closures  for this morning's procession we're  going to send it over to hector who has  a look at those so you can plan out your  day hector  hey there bianca it'll be a really  difficult day for all of our law  enforcement and the first responders  community here in the valley  so it all starts at 9 30 this morning  ndot says prepare significant delays  the procession will go from downtown  from palm mortuary starting at 9 30 this  morning  it'll get onto the i-15 get off on  spring mountain road  and then travel down las vegas boulevard  before getting on the beltway in the  south at 2 15.  eventually it will go northbound on the  95 515 over for central christian church  then right about around one o'clock in  the evening  one pm it'll basically take the same  route it'll go southbound on the 95  it'll come back on the 215 and then get  off on warm springs road  for the gravesite that starts at 1pm
 

